  "rules": {
    "S": "S(arm) = #cells where the donor-new-source patch is JOINT and the donor-ROUND-source patch of the same arm is not (target host new)",
    "SPEC": "SPEC iff dM_main > dM_round in >= 75% of cells AND in a majority of cells for >= 10 of 14 donor groups",
    "SUF": "SUF(arm) iff S(arm) >= 1/2 S(full) and SPEC(arm)",
    "always_reported": "S, SPEC, J_main, J_round and median dM per arm; per host; leave-one-donor-group-out of both verdicts; energy fraction of lr_k / rand_k; change norm of every arm relative to the full patch; all nulls",
    "consistency_gate": "full = the M3 all-heads patch: its 208 rows equal M3's bitwise and S(full) = 51; xdonor_BULK = the M5 third-donor arm: its 208 rows equal M5's bitwise and S = 51 (GPU, checked in the run); otherwise verdict INCONSISTENT_WITH_M3_M5 and no claim",
    "interpretation_fixed_in_advance": "SHARED_DONOR_COMPONENT: one averaged donor BULK contribution, from donors other than the cell's own, gives hosts the round-specific repair while the averaged BULK of other hosts does not: a donor-like shared component, not scene content. GENERIC_CONTEXT_SHIFT: any averaged context read works, so the M5 'donor-like' reading is not supported. SHARED_NEEDS_DONOR_REST: the averaged component works only together with the rest of the donor's write. NOT_SHARED_BY_AVERAGE: averaging destroys what a single third donor carries (M5 XD_HOLDS), e.g. donors agree in subspace but not in sign or position pattern. LOWRANK:k: the repairing part of delta_B lies in a k-dimensional subspace learned from other donors, and a random k-subspace of the same size does not repair. The pooled means change the host by their own size (not matched); their change norms relative to the full patch are reported. The subspace is fit on both arms (new and ROUND) of the pool donors, so round-specificity of lr_k comes from the cell's own delta_B, not from the basis",
    "lowrank_verdict": "k* = the smallest k in 1, 4, 16, 64 with SUF(lr_k); null arm = rand_max(k*, 4); NULL holds iff S(null) <= 5 and not SPEC(null). LOWRANK:k* if k* exists and NULL holds; LOWRANK_UNRESOLVED:k* if k* exists and NULL fails; NOT_LOWRANK_LE64 if no k*",
    "readouts": "M = conflict margin; A = logit(reject_conflict) - max(accept, wait); JOINT = M > 0 and A > 0; dM = M(patch) - M(in-run capture of host new)",
    "shared_verdict": "SHARED_DONOR_COMPONENT if SUF(meanD_host) and not SUF(meanH_host); GENERIC_CONTEXT_SHIFT if SUF(meanD_host) and SUF(meanH_host); SHARED_NEEDS_DONOR_REST if not SUF(meanD_host) and SUF(meanD_donor); NOT_SHARED_BY_AVERAGE otherwise",
    "size_gate": "for every rand_k row, ||patch - host|| per row and span position equals ||U_k U_k^T delta_B|| within 1e-3 relative (fail-closed in the runner); the energy fraction ||U_k U_k^T delta_B|| / ||delta_B|| is recorded in every lr_k and rand_k row",
    "units": "the 104 cross-group cells of M1-M5; cells share donors and hosts, and the pooled-mean arms vary with the donor only through the pool exclusion (effectively 8 hosts), so counts are descriptive decision rules, not independent tests; per-host S is always reported"
  },
